# Corpus files on which tree-sitter-smt2 knowingly disagrees with Z3's parser.
# Format: <path relative to corpus/><TAB><reason>
#
# After an error, Z3 skips the rest of the command, which hides any syntax
# errors there.  In these files, Z3 reports a semantic error (e.g., an unknown
# sort) before a syntax error in the same command.  cvc5's set.comprehension
# binds variables, which Z3 parses as an application without arguments, e.g.,
# ((x Int)).
./cvc5_cvc5/test/regress/cli/regress0/datatypes/issue12572-nullable-lift-no-arguments.smt2	Z3 reports a semantic error first; also ((_ nullable.lift f)) has no arguments
